# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here, we seem to have even less predictability! Previously, we at least knew what the outcome would be of the first measurement, now we have a fairly even distribution across all possible states. It's not too hard to see why this happened. We started in $|0\\rangle$, which is a 50-50 mixture of $|+\\rangle_x$ and $|-\\rangle_x$, according to\n"
"$$|0\\rangle=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|+\\rangle_x+|-\\rangle_x)$$\n"
"So clearly there should be equal probability of obtaining the + or - state (mapped to 0 and 1 in the chart) for the first measurement. The measurement along $x$ collapses the state into either an eigenstate $|+\\rangle_x$ or the eigenstate $|-\\rangle_x$. Each one of those states is a 50-50 mixture of $|0\\rangle$ and $|1\\rangle$, according to\n"
"$$|+\\rangle_x = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle)$$\n"
"$$|-\\rangle_x = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle-|1\\rangle)$$\n"
"So once the system is in an eigenstate of $x$, clearly, measurements along $z$ will yield both $|0\\rangle$ and $|1\\rangle$, and will do so with roughly equal probability.\n"
"So our first example showed us that some states will have very predictable outcomes of some measurements, but unpredictable outcomes for other measurements. The current example shows us that we can do worse than that. There are states that can give us unpredictable outcomes for both measurements, even if all we do is swap the order of the measurements. Let's investigate how certain or uncertain a quantity is for a given state.\n"
msgstr ""
"Aquí, ¡parece que tenemos aún menos predecibilidad! Antes, al menos sabíamos cuál sería el resultado de la primera medida; ahora tenemos una distribución bastante uniforme entre todos los estados posibles. No es difícil entender por qué ocurrió esto. Empezamos en $|0\\rangle$, que es una mezcla 50-50 de $|+\\rangle_x$ y $|-\\rangle_x$, según\n"
"$$|0\\rangle=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|+\\rangle_x+|-\\rangle_x)$$\n"
"Así que claramente debe haber igual probabilidad de obtener el estado + o - (mapeados a 0 y 1 en el gráfico) en la primera medida. La medida a lo largo de $x$ colapsa el estado hacia un autoestado $|+\\rangle_x$ o el autoestado $|-\\rangle_x$. Cada uno de esos estados es una mezcla 50-50 de $|0\\rangle$ y $|1\\rangle$, según\n"
"$$|+\\rangle_x = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle)$$\n"
"$$|-\\rangle_x = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle-|1\\rangle)$$\n"
"Así que una vez que el sistema está en un autoestado de $x$, claramente las medidas a lo largo de $z$ darán tanto $|0\\rangle$ como $|1\\rangle$, y lo harán con probabilidad aproximadamente igual.\n"
"Nuestro primer ejemplo nos mostró que algunos estados tendrán resultados muy predecibles para ciertas medidas, pero impredecibles para otras. El ejemplo actual nos muestra que podemos ir más allá. Hay estados que pueden darnos resultados impredecibles para ambas medidas, aunque lo único que hagamos sea invertir el orden de las medidas. Investiguemos qué tan cierta o incierta es una magnitud para un estado dado.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Calculating uncertainty {#calculating-uncertainty}"
msgstr "Calculando la incertidumbre {#calculating-uncertainty}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can quantify this using uncertainty, or variance. The \"uncertainty\" is "
"often defined to be the square root of the \"variance\" of a distribution. "
"That is, the uncertainty for some observable $S$ is denoted $\\Delta S$ and "
"is given by\n"
msgstr ""
"Podemos cuantificar esto usando la incertidumbre, o varianza. La "
"\"incertidumbre\" se define generalmente como la raíz cuadrada de la "
"\"varianza\" de una distribución. Es decir, la incertidumbre de un "
"observable $S$ se denota $\\Delta S$ y viene dada por\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"(\\Delta S)^2 & \\equiv \\langle (S - \\langle S \\rangle)^2 \\rangle\\\\\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"(\\Delta S)^2 & \\equiv \\langle (S - \\langle S \\rangle)^2 \\rangle\\\\\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(\\Delta S)^2 & = \\langle S^2 - 2 S \\langle S \\rangle +\\langle S "
"\\rangle^2 \\rangle\\\\\n"
msgstr ""
"(\\Delta S)^2 & = \\langle S^2 - 2 S \\langle S \\rangle +\\langle S "
"\\rangle^2 \\rangle\\\\\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(\\Delta S)^2 & = \\langle S^2 \\rangle - \\langle S \\rangle^2\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"(\\Delta S)^2 & = \\langle S^2 \\rangle - \\langle S \\rangle^2\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "For the case of Pauli matrices, for which $S^2 = I$, this becomes\n"
msgstr ""
"Para el caso de las matrices de Pauli, en las que $S^2 = I$, esto se "
"convierte en\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"(\\Delta S)^2 = 1 - \\langle S \\rangle^2\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"(\\Delta S)^2 = 1 - \\langle S \\rangle^2\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let's apply this to a concrete example. Let's start with the state "
"$|\\psi\\rangle = |+\\rangle_y = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\"
" i \\end{pmatrix},$ and let's determine the uncertainty of the observable "
"$X$ in that state.\n"
msgstr ""
"Apliquemos esto a un ejemplo concreto. Comencemos con el estado "
"$|\\psi\\rangle = |+\\rangle_y = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\"
" i \\end{pmatrix},$ y determinemos la incertidumbre del observable $X$ en "
"ese estado.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Check your understanding {#check-your-understanding}"
msgstr "Comprueba tu comprensión {#check-your-understanding}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Calculate the uncertainty of $X$ in the state $|+\\rangle_y = |+i\\rangle$, "
"by hand.\n"
msgstr ""
"Calcula la incertidumbre de $X$ en el estado $|+\\rangle_y = |+i\\rangle$, a"
" mano.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Answer\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Respuesta\">\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Delta X =\\sqrt{\\langle+i| X^2 |+i\\rangle - \\langle+i| X |+i\\rangle^2}\n"
"$$\n"
"In the given state, this yields:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\Delta X & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix}1 & -i\\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{pmatrix} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix}1 \\\\ i\\end{pmatrix} - \\left(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix}1 & -i\\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{pmatrix} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix}1 \\\\ i\\end{pmatrix}\\right)^2}\\\\\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Delta X =\\sqrt{\\langle+i| X^2 |+i\\rangle - \\langle+i| X |+i\\rangle^2}\n"
"$$\n"
"En el estado dado, esto produce:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\Delta X & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix}1 & -i\\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{pmatrix} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix}1 \\\\ i\\end{pmatrix} - \\left(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix}1 & -i\\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{pmatrix} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix}1 \\\\ i\\end{pmatrix}\\right)^2}\\\\\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\Delta X & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{pmatrix}1 & -i\\end{pmatrix} "
"\\begin{pmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix}1 \\\\ "
"i\\end{pmatrix} - \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{pmatrix}1 & -i\\end{pmatrix} "
"\\begin{pmatrix}i \\\\ 1\\end{pmatrix}\\right)^2}\\\\\n"
msgstr ""
"\\Delta X & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{pmatrix}1 & -i\\end{pmatrix} "
"\\begin{pmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix}1 \\\\ "
"i\\end{pmatrix} - \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{pmatrix}1 & -i\\end{pmatrix} "
"\\begin{pmatrix}i \\\\ 1\\end{pmatrix}\\right)^2}\\\\\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\Delta X & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{pmatrix}1 & -i\\end{pmatrix} "
"\\begin{pmatrix}1 \\\\ i\\end{pmatrix} - "
"\\left(\\frac{1}{2}(0))\\right)^2}\\\\\n"
msgstr ""
"\\Delta X & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{pmatrix}1 & -i\\end{pmatrix} "
"\\begin{pmatrix}1 \\\\ i\\end{pmatrix} - "
"\\left(\\frac{1}{2}(0))\\right)^2}\\\\\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\Delta X & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{2}(2)} = 1\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\Delta X & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{2}(2)} = 1\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
msgstr ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can create an arbitrary initial state using ```qc.initialize()```. Note "
"that the syntax for the imaginary unit here is $1j$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Podemos crear un estado inicial arbitrario usando ```qc.initialize()```. Ten"
" en cuenta que la sintaxis para la unidad imaginaria aquí es $1j$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"According to our equation above,\n"
"$$(\\Delta X)^2 = 1 - \\langle X \\rangle^2 = 1-(0.0015...)^2 \\rightarrow \\Delta X = 0.999...$$\n"
"Let's stick with that same state, but find the expectation value of $Z$, now:\n"
msgstr ""
"Según nuestra ecuación anterior,\n"
"$$(\\Delta X)^2 = 1 - \\langle X \\rangle^2 = 1-(0.0015...)^2 \\rightarrow \\Delta X = 0.999...$$\n"
"Mantengamos ese mismo estado, pero calculemos ahora el valor esperado de $Z$:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We could do the same math as before, but we would see that the variance is "
"again very close to 1.0. We could conclude that $\\Delta X \\Delta Z "
"\\approx 1.0$. Indeed this approximately correct for the state we chose. But"
" can we do better? Or worse?\n"
msgstr ""
"Podríamos hacer la misma operación matemática que antes, pero veríamos que "
"la varianza es de nuevo muy cercana a 1.0. Podríamos concluir que $\\Delta X"
" \\Delta Z \\approx 1.0$. Esto es aproximadamente correcto para el estado "
"que elegimos. ¿Pero podemos hacerlo mejor? ¿O peor?\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Recall that there is an uncertainty relation between position along one direction, $x,$ and momentum along the same direction, $p_x.$ For those variables, but most familiar form is probably\n"
"$$\\Delta x \\Delta p_x \\geq \\hbar/2$$\n"
"If this is all we remember, we might be tempted to think that $\\Delta X$ and $\\Delta Z$ could also have such a fundamental limit on uncertainty. Perhaps it is impossible for the product $\\Delta X \\Delta Z$ to reach zero? Let's try another state and see if this holds. This time, we'll use $|\\psi\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}.$ Let's see what happens. Note that in the code below, estimator can accept two sets of circuits and observables in the same job submission.\n"
msgstr ""
"Recuerda que existe una relación de incertidumbre entre la posición a lo largo de una dirección, $x,$ y el momento a lo largo de esa misma dirección, $p_x.$ Para esas variables, la forma más familiar es probablemente\n"
"$$\\Delta x \\Delta p_x \\geq \\hbar/2$$\n"
"Si esto es todo lo que recordamos, podríamos caer en la tentación de pensar que $\\Delta X$ y $\\Delta Z$ también podrían tener un límite fundamental similar en la incertidumbre. ¿Quizás es imposible que el producto $\\Delta X \\Delta Z$ llegue a cero? Probemos con otro estado y veamos si esto se cumple. Esta vez usaremos $|\\psi\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}.$ Veamos qué ocurre. Ten en cuenta que en el código siguiente, el estimator puede aceptar dos conjuntos de circuitos y observables en la misma entrega de trabajo.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The expectation value of $X$ should be close to 1.0, but should not exceed "
"1.0. Don't worry if it exceeds 1.0 by a very small amount. This can be "
"attributed to factors like noise and/or readout error. Although this is a "
"very important topic, we can ignore it for now.\n"
msgstr ""
"El valor esperado de $X$ debería ser cercano a 1.0, pero no debería superar "
"1.0. No te preocupes si lo supera por una cantidad muy pequeña. Esto puede "
"atribuirse a factores como el ruido y/o errores de lectura. Aunque este es "
"un tema muy importante, podemos ignorarlo por ahora.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We obtained an expectation value of $X$ that is very close to 1.0 "
"(corresponding to a very low variance for $X$). This makes the product of "
"the two variances quite low:\n"
msgstr ""
"Obtuvimos un valor esperado de $X$ muy cercano a 1.0 (correspondiente a una "
"varianza muy baja para $X$). Esto hace que el producto de las dos varianzas "
"sea bastante bajo:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Delta X \\Delta Z = \\sqrt{1-(0.9853)^2} \\times \\sqrt{1-(-0.00195)^2} = 0.171.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Delta X \\Delta Z = \\sqrt{1-(0.9853)^2} \\times \\sqrt{1-(-0.00195)^2} = 0.171.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"While this is not exactly zero, this value is getting small in comparison "
"with the eigenvalues of the Pauli operators ($\\pm 1$). Well, you may recall"
" that the uncertainty relation between linear position and momentum could be"
" written differently, explicitly using the commutation relation between the "
"operators $x$ and $p_x$:\n"
msgstr ""
"Aunque esto no es exactamente cero, este valor se está volviendo pequeño en "
"comparación con los valores propios de los operadores de Pauli ($\\pm 1$). "
"Bien, puede que recuerdes que la relación de incertidumbre entre la posición"
" lineal y el momento puede escribirse de otra forma, usando explícitamente "
"la relación de conmutación entre los operadores $x$ y $p_x$:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Delta x \\Delta p_x \\geq \\frac{1}{2}|\\langle [x,p_x] \\rangle|\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Delta x \\Delta p_x \\geq \\frac{1}{2}|\\langle [x,p_x] \\rangle|\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "where\n"
msgstr "donde\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"[x,p_x] = xp_x-p_xx\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"[x,p_x] = xp_x-p_xx\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "is the commutator of $x$ and $p_x$.\n"
msgstr "es el conmutador de $x$ y $p_x$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is the form that that can be most easily extended to the Pauli operators. Generally, for two operators $A$ and $B$,\n"
"$$\n"
"\\Delta A \\Delta B \\geq \\frac{1}{2}|\\langle [A,B] \\rangle|.\n"
"$$\n"
"And in the case of the Pauli matrices $X$ and $Z$, we need $[X,Z]$ in order to calculate\n"
"$$\n"
"\\Delta X \\Delta Z \\geq \\frac{1}{2}|\\langle [X,Z] \\rangle|.\n"
"$$\n"
"We show this here, and leave similar calculations to the reader as an exercise:\n"
"$$\n"
"[X,Z] = XZ-ZX = \\begin{pmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{pmatrix}-\\begin{pmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
"$$\n"
"[X,Z] = \\begin{pmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{pmatrix}-\\begin{pmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{pmatrix} = 2\\begin{pmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
"This is a perfectly acceptable answer, but with one more step, we see\n"
msgstr ""
"Esta es la forma que más fácilmente puede extenderse a los operadores de Pauli. En general, para dos operadores $A$ y $B$,\n"
"$$\n"
"\\Delta A \\Delta B \\geq \\frac{1}{2}|\\langle [A,B] \\rangle|.\n"
"$$\n"
"Y en el caso de las matrices de Pauli $X$ y $Z$, necesitamos $[X,Z]$ para calcular\n"
"$$\n"
"\\Delta X \\Delta Z \\geq \\frac{1}{2}|\\langle [X,Z] \\rangle|.\n"
"$$\n"
"Mostramos esto a continuación y dejamos cálculos similares al lector como ejercicio:\n"
"$$\n"
"[X,Z] = XZ-ZX = \\begin{pmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{pmatrix}-\\begin{pmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
"$$\n"
"[X,Z] = \\begin{pmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{pmatrix}-\\begin{pmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{pmatrix} = 2\\begin{pmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
"Esta es una respuesta perfectamente válida, pero con un paso más vemos que\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"[X,Z] = -2i\\begin{pmatrix}0 & -i \\\\ i & 0\\end{pmatrix}=-2iY\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"[X,Z] = -2i\\begin{pmatrix}0 & -i \\\\ i & 0\\end{pmatrix}=-2iY\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Our uncertainty relation thus becomes\n"
msgstr "Nuestra relación de incertidumbre se convierte entonces en\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Delta X \\Delta Z \\geq |\\langle Y \\rangle|.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Delta X \\Delta Z \\geq |\\langle Y \\rangle|.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Check your understanding {#check-your-understanding-1}"
msgstr "Comprueba tu comprensión {#check-your-understanding-1}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Determine $[X,Y]$ and $[Y,Z]$. Use this to write down the uncertainty "
"relations between $X$ & $Y$, and $Y$ & $Z$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Determina $[X,Y]$ y $[Y,Z]$. Usa esto para escribir las relaciones de "
"incertidumbre entre $X$ & $Y$, y entre $Y$ & $Z$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"[X,Y] = XY-YX = \\begin{pmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}0 & -i \\\\ i & 0\\end{pmatrix}-\\begin{pmatrix}0 & -i \\\\ i & 0\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{pmatrix} = 2 \\begin{pmatrix}i & 0 \\\\ 0 & -i\\end{pmatrix}=2iZ\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"[X,Y] = XY-YX = \\begin{pmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}0 & -i \\\\ i & 0\\end{pmatrix}-\\begin{pmatrix}0 & -i \\\\ i & 0\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{pmatrix} = 2 \\begin{pmatrix}i & 0 \\\\ 0 & -i\\end{pmatrix}=2iZ\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"[Y,Z] = YZ-ZY = \\begin{pmatrix}0 & -i \\\\ i & 0\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{pmatrix}-\\begin{pmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}0 & -i \\\\ i & 0\\end{pmatrix} = 2 \\begin{pmatrix}0 & i \\\\ i & 0\\end{pmatrix}=2iX\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"[Y,Z] = YZ-ZY = \\begin{pmatrix}0 & -i \\\\ i & 0\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{pmatrix}-\\begin{pmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}0 & -i \\\\ i & 0\\end{pmatrix} = 2 \\begin{pmatrix}0 & i \\\\ i & 0\\end{pmatrix}=2iX\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Combining with the general uncertainty relation, we have\n"
"$$\n"
"\\Delta X \\Delta Y \\geq |\\langle Z \\rangle|,\n"
"$$\n"
"$$\n"
"\\Delta Y \\Delta Z \\geq |\\langle X \\rangle|.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Combinando con la relación de incertidumbre general, tenemos\n"
"$$\n"
"\\Delta X \\Delta Y \\geq |\\langle Z \\rangle|,\n"
"$$\n"
"$$\n"
"\\Delta Y \\Delta Z \\geq |\\langle X \\rangle|.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Verify consistency {#verify-consistency}"
msgstr "Verificar consistencia {#verify-consistency}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Before moving on, let us check that this was consistent with our previous finding. We used the state $|\\psi\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}.$ And we found that $\\Delta X \\Delta Z  = 0.171.$ Now we know this product should be greater than or equal to\n"
"$$\n"
"|\\langle Y \\rangle|=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 1 \\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}0 & -i \\\\ i & 0\\end{pmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
"$$\n"
"|\\langle Y \\rangle| = \\frac{1}{2}\\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 1 \\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix} -i \\\\ i \\end{pmatrix} = \\frac{1}{2}(-i+i) = 0.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Antes de continuar, comprobemos que esto fue consistente con nuestro hallazgo anterior. Usamos el estado $|\\psi\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}.$ Y encontramos que $\\Delta X \\Delta Z  = 0.171.$ Ahora sabemos que este producto debería ser mayor o igual que\n"
"$$\n"
"|\\langle Y \\rangle|=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 1 \\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}0 & -i \\\\ i & 0\\end{pmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
"$$\n"
"|\\langle Y \\rangle| = \\frac{1}{2}\\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 1 \\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix} -i \\\\ i \\end{pmatrix} = \\frac{1}{2}(-i+i) = 0.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"So indeed, $\\Delta X \\Delta Z  = 0.171 \\geq |\\langle Y \\rangle|=0$\n"
"Use the questions below to build some intuition for these findings:\n"
msgstr ""
"Efectivamente, $\\Delta X \\Delta Z  = 0.171 \\geq |\\langle Y \\rangle|=0$\n"
"Usa las preguntas a continuación para desarrollar intuición sobre estos resultados:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Check your understanding {#check-your-understanding-2}"
msgstr "Comprueba tu comprensión {#check-your-understanding-2}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Answer the following items together as a set:\n"
msgstr "Responde los siguientes puntos en conjunto:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "(a) What states would you expect to have zero uncertainty in $X$?\n"
msgstr "(a) ¿Para qué estados esperarías tener incertidumbre cero en $X$?\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "(b) What states would you expect to have zero uncertainty in $Z$?\n"
msgstr "(b) ¿Para qué estados esperarías tener incertidumbre cero en $Z$?\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(c) In what states would you obtain a zero expectation value $\\langle Y "
"\\rangle$?\n"
msgstr ""
"(c) ¿En qué estados obtendrías un valor esperado $\\langle Y \\rangle$ igual"
" a cero?\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(d) Are the answers to the above questions consistent with the case $\\Delta"
" X \\Delta Z \\geq |\\langle Y \\rangle|$?\n"
msgstr ""
"(d) ¿Son consistentes las respuestas anteriores con el caso $\\Delta X "
"\\Delta Z \\geq |\\langle Y \\rangle|$?\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "(e) Write code to explicitly check this using estimator.\n"
msgstr ""
"(e) Escribe código para verificar esto explícitamente usando estimator.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(a) We might expect eigenstates of the $X$ operator to yield zero uncertainty in $X$. Indeed, using $|\\psi\\rangle = |+\\rangle_x,$ we have\n"
"$$\\Delta X = \\sqrt{1-\\langle X \\rangle^2} = \\sqrt{1-1^2} = 0.$$\n"
msgstr ""
"(a) Podríamos esperar que los estados propios del operador $X$ produzcan incertidumbre cero en $X$. En efecto, usando $|\\psi\\rangle = |+\\rangle_x,$ tenemos\n"
"$$\\Delta X = \\sqrt{1-\\langle X \\rangle^2} = \\sqrt{1-1^2} = 0.$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(b) We might expect eigenstates of the $Z$ operator to yield zero uncertainty in $Z$. Indeed, using $|\\psi\\rangle = |1\\rangle,$ we have\n"
"$$\\Delta Z = \\sqrt{1-\\langle Z \\rangle^2} = \\sqrt{1-(-1)^2} = 0.$$\n"
msgstr ""
"(b) Podríamos esperar que los estados propios del operador $Z$ produzcan incertidumbre cero en $Z$. En efecto, usando $|\\psi\\rangle = |1\\rangle,$ tenemos\n"
"$$\\Delta Z = \\sqrt{1-\\langle Z \\rangle^2} = \\sqrt{1-(-1)^2} = 0.$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(c) We expect to find $\\langle Y \\rangle=0$ for any states that, when "
"measured, yield a positive projection on the $y$ axis just as often as a "
"negative projection. These include the eigenstates of $X$ and $Z$.\n"
msgstr ""
"(c) Esperamos encontrar $\\langle Y \\rangle=0$ para cualquier estado que, "
"al medirse, produzca una proyección positiva sobre el eje $y$ con la misma "
"frecuencia que una negativa. Esto incluye los estados propios de $X$ y "
"$Z$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(d) Yes. One would expect a very small value for the product of "
"uncertainties $\\Delta X \\Delta Z $ for eigenstates of $X$ or $Z$: $\\Delta"
" X \\Delta Z \\approx 0.$ This can hold because we would also expect "
"$\\langle Y \\rangle=0$ for those same states. So the uncertainty relation "
"could be satisfied.\n"
msgstr ""
"(d) Sí. Cabría esperar un valor muy pequeño para el producto de "
"incertidumbres $\\Delta X \\Delta Z $ en los estados propios de $X$ o $Z$: "
"$\\Delta X \\Delta Z \\approx 0.$ Esto puede cumplirse porque también "
"esperaríamos $\\langle Y \\rangle=0$ para esos mismos estados. Así que la "
"relación de incertidumbre podría satisfacerse.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "(e) Code such as the following would verify this:\n"
msgstr "(e) Un código como el siguiente permitiría verificarlo:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Where the results returns all expectation values. To retrieve all "
"expectation values and calculate uncertainties, we could use:\n"
msgstr ""
"Donde el resultado devuelve todos los valores esperados. Para recuperar "
"todos los valores esperados y calcular las incertidumbres, podríamos usar:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(a) Can you think of a state in which you would have a large expectation "
"value $\\langle Y \\rangle$?\n"
msgstr ""
"(a) ¿Puedes pensar en un estado en el que tendrías un valor esperado "
"$\\langle Y \\rangle$ grande?\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(b) Would you expect that same state to have large or small uncertainty in "
"$X$?\n"
msgstr ""
"(b) ¿Esperarías que ese mismo estado tenga una incertidumbre grande o "
"pequeña en $X$?\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(c) Would you expect that same state to have large or small uncertainty in "
"$Z$?\n"
msgstr ""
"(c) ¿Esperarías que ese mismo estado tenga una incertidumbre grande o "
"pequeña en $Z$?\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(a) We expect to find $\\langle Y \\rangle\\approx 1$ for the eigenstate of "
"$Y$: $|+\\rangle_y$.\n"
msgstr ""
"(a) Esperamos encontrar $\\langle Y \\rangle\\approx 1$ para el estado "
"propio de $Y$: $|+\\rangle_y$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(b) We might expect $X$ to have large uncertainty in the state "
"$|+\\rangle_y,$ since measuring $X$ in that state would yield a positive and"
" negative result with equal frequency/probability.\n"
msgstr ""
"(b) Podríamos esperar que $X$ tenga una incertidumbre grande en el estado "
"$|+\\rangle_y,$ ya que medir $X$ en ese estado produciría un resultado "
"positivo y uno negativo con igual frecuencia/probabilidad.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(c) We might expect $Z$ to have large uncertainty in the state "
"$|+\\rangle_y,$ since measuring $Z$ in that state would yield a positive and"
" negative result with equal frequency/probability.\n"
msgstr ""
"(c) Podríamos esperar que $Z$ tenga una incertidumbre grande en el estado "
"$|+\\rangle_y,$ ya que medir $Z$ en ese estado produciría un resultado "
"positivo y uno negativo con igual frecuencia/probabilidad.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(d) Yes. One would expect a large value for the product of uncertainties "
"$\\Delta X \\Delta Z $ for eigenstates of $Y,$ and for $|+\\rangle_y,$ "
"specifically. We would also expect $\\langle Y \\rangle\\approx 1$ for that "
"same state. So both $\\langle Y \\rangle$ and $\\Delta X \\Delta Z $ are "
"both fairly large in this state, and it is plausible that the uncertainty "
"relation could again be satisfied.\n"
msgstr ""
"(d) Sí. Cabría esperar un valor grande para el producto de incertidumbres "
"$\\Delta X \\Delta Z $ en los estados propios de $Y,$ y en particular para "
"$|+\\rangle_y$. También esperaríamos $\\langle Y \\rangle\\approx 1$ para "
"ese mismo estado. Por tanto, tanto $\\langle Y \\rangle$ como $\\Delta X "
"\\Delta Z $ son bastante grandes en ese estado, y es plausible que la "
"relación de incertidumbre vuelva a satisfacerse.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Testing uncertainty relations {#testing-uncertainty-relations}"
msgstr ""
"Probando las relaciones de incertidumbre {#testing-uncertainty-relations}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The test above only demonstrated the validity of the uncertainty relation "
"for a single choice of state vector $|\\psi\\rangle = |+\\rangle_x$. To "
"convince ourselves that this is generally consistent with experiment, we "
"should carry out similar calculations using estimator for many choices of "
"the state vector. Let's start by rotating our state vector away from the $z$"
" axis, using an ```RY``` gate to produce different initial states using a "
"parameter $\\theta$.\n"
msgstr ""
"La prueba anterior solo demostró la validez de la relación de incertidumbre "
"para una única elección del vector de estado $|\\psi\\rangle = "
"|+\\rangle_x$. Para convencernos de que esto es generalmente consistente con"
" el experimento, deberíamos realizar cálculos similares usando el estimador "
"para muchas elecciones del vector de estado. Empecemos rotando nuestro "
"vector de estado alejándolo del eje $z$, usando una puerta ```RY``` para "
"producir distintos estados iniciales mediante un parámetro $\\theta$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/modules/quantum-"
"mechanics/exploring-uncertainty-with-qiskit/extracted-"
"outputs/1599d4df-38f8-4171-95ae-6c3c61409201-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Salida de la celda de código anterior](/learning/images/modules/quantum-"
"mechanics/exploring-uncertainty-with-qiskit/extracted-"
"outputs/1599d4df-38f8-4171-95ae-6c3c61409201-0.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Note that the red curve $(\\Delta X \\Delta Z)$ is always greater than the "
"orange curve $\\langle Y \\rangle.$ Sometimes the uncertainty product dips "
"and is somewhat close to the limit, and other times it rises and is farther "
"from the limit, but it always obeys the uncertainty relation.\n"
msgstr ""
"Observa que la curva roja $(\\Delta X \\Delta Z)$ es siempre mayor que la "
"curva naranja $\\langle Y \\rangle.$ A veces el producto de incertidumbre "
"desciende y se acerca bastante al límite, y otras veces sube y se aleja más "
"del límite, pero siempre obedece la relación de incertidumbre.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Of course, this might not be the best test of the uncertainty relation, "
"since our limit $\\langle Y \\rangle$ is always very close to zero. Let's "
"use a quantum state that has a larger projection on eigenstates of $Y$. "
"Specifically, we will still rotate rotate $|0\\rangle$ down from the $z$ "
"axis by varying angles, but now we will also rotate that resulting state "
"around $z$ by some angle, perhaps $\\pi/4$, and see what happens.\n"
msgstr ""
"Por supuesto, esta puede no ser la mejor prueba de la relación de "
"incertidumbre, ya que nuestro límite $\\langle Y \\rangle$ está siempre muy "
"cercano a cero. Usemos un estado cuántico que tenga una proyección mayor "
"sobre los autoestados de $Y$. En concreto, seguiremos rotando $|0\\rangle$ "
"hacia abajo desde el eje $z$ con ángulos variables, pero ahora también "
"rotaremos ese estado resultante alrededor de $z$ un cierto ángulo, quizás "
"$\\pi/4$, y veremos qué ocurre.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/modules/quantum-"
"mechanics/exploring-uncertainty-with-qiskit/extracted-"
"outputs/6f129a2d-e029-45b7-bb77-bfa83babd8c9-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Salida de la celda de código anterior](/learning/images/modules/quantum-"
"mechanics/exploring-uncertainty-with-qiskit/extracted-"
"outputs/6f129a2d-e029-45b7-bb77-bfa83babd8c9-0.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now we see that the limit on the uncertainty $(\\Delta X \\Delta Z)$ is "
"being put to the test! The red curve comes much closer to the orange curve "
"than before. In fact, in the absence of noise, the uncertainty relation "
"would be exactly saturated ($(\\Delta X \\Delta Z) = \\langle Y \\rangle$) "
"one point. In the presence of noise and readout error, it should not be "
"surprising if a run occasionally yields $(\\Delta X \\Delta Z)$ very "
"slightly larger than $\\langle Y \\rangle.$ This is not a true violation of "
"uncertainty; it is just an artifact of non-zero error.\n"
msgstr ""
"¡Ahora vemos que el límite sobre la incertidumbre $(\\Delta X \\Delta Z)$ "
"está siendo puesto a prueba! La curva roja se acerca mucho más a la curva "
"naranja que antes. De hecho, en ausencia de ruido, la relación de "
"incertidumbre quedaría exactamente saturada ($(\\Delta X \\Delta Z) = "
"\\langle Y \\rangle$) en un punto. En presencia de ruido y error de lectura,"
" no debería sorprendernos que una ejecución ocasionalmente arroje un valor "
"de $(\\Delta X \\Delta Z)$ ligeramente mayor que $\\langle Y \\rangle.$ Esto"
" no es una violación real de la incertidumbre; es simplemente un artefacto "
"de un error no nulo.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Check your understanding {#check-your-understanding-3}"
msgstr ""

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
