# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Critical concepts: {#critical-concepts}"
msgstr "Conceptos clave: {#critical-concepts}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There are uncertainty relations between many sets of physical observables, "
"including position & linear momentum, and components of spin.\n"
msgstr ""
"Existen relaciones de incertidumbre entre muchos conjuntos de observables "
"físicos, incluyendo la posición y el momento lineal, y las componentes del "
"espín.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Pauli matrices do not commute. This is a mathematical reflection of the "
"fact that not all components of spin can be simultaneously "
"known/determined.\n"
msgstr ""
"Las matrices de Pauli no conmutan. Esto es un reflejo matemático del hecho "
"de que no todas las componentes del espín pueden conocerse/determinarse "
"simultáneamente.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Quantum computing makes heavy use of the Pauli operators/matrices, so it is "
"useful to know the uncertainty relation for Pauli operators, as well as the "
"closely-related spin operators.\n"
msgstr ""
"La computación cuántica hace un uso intensivo de los operadores/matrices de "
"Pauli, por lo que resulta útil conocer la relación de incertidumbre para los"
" operadores de Pauli, así como los operadores de espín estrechamente "
"relacionados.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A general formula for the uncertainty of two operators $A$ and $B$ is "
"$$\\Delta A \\Delta B \\geq \\frac{1}{2}|\\langle [A,B] \\rangle|.$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Una fórmula general para la incertidumbre de dos operadores $A$ y $B$ es "
"$$\\Delta A \\Delta B \\geq \\frac{1}{2}|\\langle [A,B] \\rangle|.$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"An eigenstate $|a\\rangle$ of some operator $A$ yields zero uncertainty in "
"the physical observable associated with that operator. Even experimentally, "
"$\\Delta A \\approx 0.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Un autoestado $|a\\rangle$ de algún operador $A$ produce incertidumbre cero "
"en el observable físico asociado a ese operador. Incluso experimentalmente, "
"$\\Delta A \\approx 0.$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"An eigenstate $|a\\rangle$ of some operator $A$ will yield a larger "
"uncertainty for an operator $B$ that does not commute with $A$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Un autoestado $|a\\rangle$ de algún operador $A$ producirá una mayor "
"incertidumbre para un operador $B$ que no conmute con $A$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Experimental results using a real quantum computer confirm the intuition we "
"gain from matrix representations of physical operators.\n"
msgstr ""
"Los resultados experimentales obtenidos con un ordenador cuántico real "
"confirman la intuición que obtenemos de las representaciones matriciales de "
"los operadores físicos.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "T/F Questions: {#tf-questions}"
msgstr "Preguntas V/F: {#tf-questions}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "T/F One can simultaneously measure $X$ and $Y$, but not $Z$.\n"
msgstr "V/F Se pueden medir $X$ e $Y$ simultáneamente, pero no $Z$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
